mono.vendor/patches/luau-lsp-dotted-enum-types.patch

Make `local face: Enum.NormalId` resolve in the editor.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH AND NOT A DEFINITIONS FILE
    Luau resolves a dotted type through `importedTypeBindings["Enum"]["NormalId"]`.
    That map is written by `require` and by a host that reaches into the frontend;
    `parseDeclaration` and `parseTypeAlias` both call `parseName`, a single
    identifier, so no `declare` statement can produce a dotted name and no spelling
    of `mono.engine/script/bindings/engine.d.luau` can reach the map.
    `mono.tools/scriptcheck` registers the prefix itself, which is why `just
    typecheck` accepts a dotted annotation the editor otherwise underlines. This
    patch is that same registration, on luau-lsp's side of the same definitions
    file.

WHY IT IS CARRIED HERE RATHER THAN UPSTREAM OR IN A FORK
    It keys on `Enum_`, which is this engine's generator convention and nobody
    else's, so there is nothing to send upstream. `mono.vendor/AGENTS.md` names
    this file as the third shape and says why a fork was not taken.

WHERE IT GOES
    `WorkspaceFolder::loadDefinitionFile`, immediately after the two
    `mutateRegisteredDefinitions` calls — one hunk, pure insertion, no header
    touched. The hook it sits beside is `LSPPlatform::mutateRegisteredDefinitions`,
    and `RobloxPlatform`'s override ends with the identical operation against an
    API dump. Overriding the hook for a platform of our own would work equally
    well and costs a header edit and a second file; this is the shape that
    conflicts least when upstream moves.

WHEN IT STOPS APPLYING
    `just luau-lsp` fails and prints this path. Re-point the hunk at whatever
    `loadDefinitionFile` looks like then; if the hook has been removed outright,
    the entry to reopen is `docs/retired/DEFERRED.md` D00031.

    A submodule pointer bump re-checks-out the tree and drops the patch. That is
    fine and is the reason the recipe applies it every run rather than once:
    the next `just luau-lsp` puts it back, or stops because it no longer fits.

diff --git a/src/Workspace.cpp b/src/Workspace.cpp
index b756435..864218d 100644
--- a/src/Workspace.cpp
+++ b/src/Workspace.cpp
@@ -515,6 +515,41 @@ Luau::LoadDefinitionFileResult WorkspaceFolder::loadDefinitionFile(
     platform->mutateRegisteredDefinitions(frontend.globals, metadata);
     platform->mutateRegisteredDefinitions(frontend.globalsForAutocomplete, metadata);
 
+    // atomic-game-engine: make `Enum.NormalId` resolve in a type position.
+    //
+    // Luau resolves a dotted type through `importedTypeBindings["Enum"]["NormalId"]`,
+    // and that map is written by `require` and by a host — never by a `declare`
+    // statement, which only ever produces a flat `exportedTypeBindings` entry. So
+    // the engine's generated definitions can declare `Enum_NormalId` and nothing
+    // else; the prefix has to be registered here. `mono.tools/scriptcheck` does
+    // exactly this loop against its own frontend, which is why the build accepts a
+    // dotted annotation that the editor otherwise underlines.
+    //
+    // The rename matches what `RobloxPlatform::mutateRegisteredDefinitions` does for
+    // its own enums in `src/platform/roblox/RobloxLuauExt.cpp`: the binding is still
+    // keyed by the flat name, so both spellings resolve, but hover and every
+    // diagnostic print the dotted one.
+    {
+        constexpr std::string_view enumPrefix = "Enum_";
+        const auto aliasDottedEnums = [&](Luau::GlobalTypes& globals)
+        {
+            if (!globals.globalScope)
+                return;
+            auto& imported = globals.globalScope->importedTypeBindings["Enum"];
+            for (const auto& [name, binding] : globals.globalScope->exportedTypeBindings)
+            {
+                if (name.size() <= enumPrefix.size() || name.compare(0, enumPrefix.size(), enumPrefix) != 0)
+                    continue;
+                std::string shortName = name.substr(enumPrefix.size());
+                if (auto* ctv = Luau::getMutable<Luau::ExternType>(binding.type))
+                    ctv->name = "Enum." + shortName;
+                imported[std::move(shortName)] = binding;
+            }
+        };
+        aliasDottedEnums(frontend.globals);
+        aliasDottedEnums(frontend.globalsForAutocomplete);
+    }
+
     if (result.success)
     {
         TextDocument textDocument(Uri(), "luau", 0, source);
